; ted-makecop-allocmem (#366): makecop (the colour gradient of the title
; bar) passes its UCopList, AllocMem(12, MEMF_PUBLIC|MEMF_CLEAR), to
; UCopperListInit and the CWait/CMove/CBump calls without testing it.
; TED alone under inject: the 2nd AllocMem of 12 bytes with exactly
; these flags, makecop's, fails (the 1st, made earlier in the start, can
; fail without harm).  QUIT.
; Correct: TED runs without the gradient and ends normally (return code
; 0); the original writes through the null pointer (low memory, the
; ExecBase pointer at address 4) and crashes.
; @source none
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject allocfail=12-12/f=10001/1+1 blitz2:ted
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=0"
timeout 20
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
